WEBVTT

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.260
Hey, Mom...

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.200
Does this mean I won't
get to see Papa anymore?

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.340
No.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.630
You won't see him every day, 
but you'll see him every now and then.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.110
"Every now and then..."

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.530
I'm sorry, Hikaru.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.580
But your father and I discussed it
and we decided to do it this way,

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.910
so that you don't get lonely.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:23.480
Mom?

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:24.720
Yes?

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.640
You remember how you said I could 
either keep my current surname, Satou,

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.970
or change it to Sakaguchi instead?

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:37.700
Would it be okay if I kept 
my name as Satou Hikaru?

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.260
Huh?

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.580
I mean, Papa's the one 
who's gonna be all alone.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.330
That's so sad.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:49.060
I want to show he was part of our family,
even if it's only by keeping his name.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:55.010
That way, I'll also never forget 
that I am my father's son.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.180
Never, ever.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.050
This room's so bright.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.070
I'll have to ask for some curtains.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:17.380
Sakaguchi

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.880
I'm digging in!

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:20.240
Ah, you have quite an appetite today!

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:24.240
Yes, I'm famished because 
I didn't finish my dinner last night.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.970
Ha, I see. If you want, 
you can have mine, too.

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:29.360
What? Really?

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:30.930
Lucky!

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:37.910
I'm off!

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:39.140
Have a good day.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.590
Take care out there.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:41.290
I will!

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.450
Hikaru's really perked up.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.420
He even wolfed down his breakfast today.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.940
<i>I can't keep being all gloomy around them.</i>

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:01.560
<i>Mom's got enough to worry about with 
the housework and looking after Grandma.</i>

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:05.300
<i>I have to hurry up and 
get used to my new life here.</i>

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:42.490
Hikaru's Feelings

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:42.790
Hey...

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:48.160
Is it true that your dad is Satou Toshiya, 
the former major leaguer?

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:49.790
Yeah, it's true.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:55.300
That's amazing! Then, that means 
you must be good at baseball, too, right?

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.040
Are you going to join our local team?

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.500
Nah, not planning on it.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.820
What? Why not?

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:03.300
I'm just not that into baseball.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.830
Then, wanna join the soccer team?

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:06.940
No, you <i>have</i> to join it!

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:09.310
You'd be a regular from day one!

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:13.190
I'm sorry. That kind of thing just 
doesn't excite me right now.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.960
Oh... I see.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.110
Oh, can we use the school yard today?

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:28.450
All right!

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.260
Second, what are you playing at?

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:32.210
The tournament's just round the corner!

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:33.810
S-Sorry.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:38.670
All right.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:39.880
I'm home!

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:44.250
How's it going, Hikaru?
You making new friends?

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.650
Yeah, slowly but surely.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:50.180
But everyone keeps asking 
what was cool in Kanagawa.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:53.290
I can't answer that,
because I was only there for three weeks.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.220
I see.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:57.430
But I think it'll all work out just fine.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.830
The school yard's bigger than 
it was in my last school,

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:02.040
and my teacher has a funny side.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.320
Oh-ho, that's good.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:06.420
Thanks for the food! It was yummy!

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:08.860
What about your bath? 
Do you want to take one now?

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.220
I'll take one when I've finished my homework.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:13.330
I see.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.800
There's no need to worry 
when he's that upbeat.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:20.790
He'll get used to his new situation soon.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:21.680
Yeah...

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:36.410
<i>I have to hurry up and forget it all.</i>

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:39.280
<i>I can't go back to Kanagawa.</i>

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.930
<i>It's going to be okay. I'll get by just fine.</i>

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.840
<i>I've managed fine up to this point.</i>

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:49.400
There!

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:53.890
Hey, Papa, can I become 
a baseball player, just like you?

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:57.550
Of course you can. I'm a champion!

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.850
All right, you two, look this way!

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.100
Champion!

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:06.540
Papa, why are you going to live
in a different house?

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:08.330
When will I see you next?

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:09.640
Maybe next month.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:12.110
I'm sorry, Hikaru.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:13.440
Okay.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:15.480
Take care of your mother, you hear?

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:16.380
Okay.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:32.540
Hey, Hikaru.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:35.260
If you want to play baseball...

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.800
I don't.

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:41.070
Soccer and basketball are <i>way</i> more fun,
so it doesn't interest me at all.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:44.690
Where do you want to go today?

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.980
Hmm, I don't know.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:50.060
If you want, we can go play catch.

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:52.360
Nothing wrong with 
working up a sweat, right?

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:58.370
Uh, there's actually a movie 
I'd like to see, instead.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:07:59.920
Oh, okay.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:08.920
Baseball?

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.400
Yep. Just so I can say I've done it 
before I get to middle school.

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:16.300
In Japan, you only get to
join one team, right?

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:19.800
If I never play baseball,
it will stick out like a sore thumb.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:22.080
I'm just trying it out, you know?

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:28.790
I have to do my homework.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:33.630
Nice ball.

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:36.820
Next, low and away.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.620
Nah, let's leave it there for today.

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:43.000
We still need to practice our trump card.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:45.630
What? O-Our trump card?

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:47.880
You seriously want to pull that out?!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.250
Of course!

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:50.960
You wanna lose or what?

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:55.010
We need to do everything we can to win.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:56.850
All right, fine.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.680
Mifune 
Batting Center

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:03.480
Home 
run

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:06.350
Fast balls

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:06.350
For both 
batting 
positions

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:06.350
Right-handed 
pitcher

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:06.350
Okay. You're getting quite good.

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:10.730
Your form still needs a lot of work,
but you're making much better contact now.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:14.150
Ah... My form still needs a lot of work, huh?

00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:15.360
Of course.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:20.980
You can't find an ideal form
 that suits you perfectly overnight.

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:25.760
Anyway, for your match this weekend,
the important thing is to make contact.

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:30.940
Don't sweat the small stuff, like form. 
Just focus on getting bat on ball.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.380
Yes, sir!

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:36.510
All right. That concludes my 
coaching sessions with you guys.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:37.470
What?

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:41.340
No way! I wanted to learn 
so much more from you.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:44.250
I've taught you the basics, so you'll be fine.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:48.250
From now until match day,
prepare by going back over all our lessons.

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:52.020
If I can fit it into my schedule, 
I'll come by on Sunday to cheer you on.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.150
Good luck, you two!

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:57.190
Thank you very much!

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:01.980
I think I'll hit a few more balls.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:04.160
Then, I'll do the same!

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:04.940
Huh?

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:08.040
Aw man, I wanted to train by myself.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.760
Hello? Yeah, it's been a while.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:21.510
Hikaru did what?

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:23.200
Right.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:25.140
Okay. Sure.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:27.130
I understand. Later.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:35.110
I apologize for calling you out of the blue.

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:41.490
Am I speaking to the manager of
the Mifune Dolphins, Tashiro-san?

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:45.110
My name is Satou Toshiya.

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.220
We're going to be late for swimming.

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.930
We'll get in trouble!

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:18.460
Papa!

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.200
Wh-What's going on?

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.950
What's brought you out to Gunma?

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.700
I wanted to come talk to you.

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.570
Huh? Y-You can't.

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:29.450
If Mom finds out that
the two of us met, she'll—

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:31.140
It's fine.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.740
It was your mother who asked me to come here.

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:37.420
She told me you'd been down in 
the dumps ever since you got here.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:41.300
Who, me? That's not true...

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:44.800
Hikaru. Why don't we go for a drive?

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.720
I'm home!

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:58.760
Daigo!

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:01.020
Perfect!

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:03.570
Can you go to Izumi's school 
real quick for me?

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:05.370
Huh? Why?

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.520
I just got a text from her.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:10.510
Her baseball team has 
a training match after school,

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:13.190
but she forgot her cleats, so she 
asked me to take them to her.

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:14.470
What?

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:18.440
No way. I was just about to 
head down to the batting center.

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:20.420
And it was you she asked, not me.

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:21.810
Pretty please.

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:25.720
I have to go to the post office.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.290
Thank god you made it in time.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:33.240
I wasn't expecting you! Thanks!

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:34.620
You'd better treat me for this.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.480
Sure, sure, at some point.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:37.650
Jeez...

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:41.950
You're free right now, right? You can
watch our match from the sidelines.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.450
Huh? I <i>do</i> have stuff to do, <i>actually!</i>

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.030
I was about to head down 
to the batting center.

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:48.570
Huh...

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:50.240
Well, it's no skin off my nose,

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:54.860
but I figured it'd be useful to watch 
a higher league match, you know?

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:56.560
Observing is training, too.

00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:58.370
Thank you!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.820
"Higher league," my ass. 
Who does she think she is?

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:04.000
It's just a training match.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:05.660
Play ball!

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:10.150
Strike!

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.000
Ball!

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:18.710
Foul!

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:32.870
Strike three! Yer out!

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.800
Nice pitch!

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:40.590
<i>She's rubbing it in.</i>

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:42.600
Strike!

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:49.170
<i>Yeah, yeah. I was supposed to be
a pitcher in the same vein, too.</i>

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.160
Izumi, nice pitching!

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:53.760
That's Shigeno Goro's DNA for ya!

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:59.060
<i>Shut up! Excuse me for 
getting the crappy genes!</i>

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:03.280
Out!

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:05.360
Two outs!

00:14:06.140 --> 00:14:08.800
<i>I guess a catcher has to
keep talking to his team.</i>

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.060
I'm sorry.

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:17.780
That scared me.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.480
So how is it here?

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:26.460
Have you made any friends?

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:29.430
W-Well, not really.

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:30.300
I see.

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:33.910
Why did Mom say I was down in the dumps?

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:36.840
I didn't think I looked down at all.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:38.260
Because she's your parent.

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:38.940
Huh?

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:42.040
Parents are always 
watching their children.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:43.770
They can tell.

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:48.380
I think I told you this before,

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:52.110
but from about your age now,

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:57.120
I started living with my grandparents
instead of my parents.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.750
For me, my grandma and 
grandpa <i>were</i> my parents.

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:03.420
Middle school graduation was coming up,

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.030
and I didn't know which 
high school I wanted to go to.

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:09.760
If I went to this one private school, 
known for its baseball expertise,

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:13.760
it would put a strain on my grandparents, 
who were on the breadline.

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:18.090
That's why I thought I'd give up 
on that idea without telling them.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:24.400
So, Toshiya, have you decided which 
high school you want to go to?

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:26.290
Yeah.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.150
I'm going to follow the crowd
and go to Mifune.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:32.360
Mifune? Are you sure?

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.410
You could go to a school 
with a stronger baseball team.

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:38.480
You're overestimating my abilities.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.300
Mifune's fine, really.

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:43.080
My friends are all going there, too.

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:47.920
Prospectus

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:52.000
Your grandma found this in your room.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:55.800
Kaidou High is famous 
for its baseball team.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:58.930
Why?

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:01.520
Why are you holding back for our sake?

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.710
Is it because we're useless old fogies?

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:08.160
Or is it just because 
we're not your real parents?

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:09.860
Grandpa...

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:13.030
Darling, I'm sure Toshiya didn't mean to—

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:15.100
It's okay to be selfish!

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:19.740
Kids are <i>supposed</i> to fight their parents
over the path they want to take in life!

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:29.380
Prospectus

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.420
Go to Kaidou!

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:29.380
You have a friend who cares 
a lot about you and about baseball, too.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:32.340
Go to Kaidou with him.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:35.460
You don't have to worry 
about how we'll fund it.

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:40.130
Money pales in comparison to your dreams.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:46.670
Thank you, Grandpa, Grandma.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:54.060
When it's for your kids, you want to help
as much as possible, whatever it is.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:55.780
That's what parents are like.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:17:02.000
I bet your mom figured out you were sad
because she's always watching out for you.

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:11.980
Yup, here's good. We'll play here.

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:14.310
Huh? Play what?

00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:19.130
Catch, of course.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.470
We haven't played in ages.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.030
Ball four!

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:38.160
<i>One out, runners on first and second.</i>

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:40.290
<i>I guess even she gets tired...</i>

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:47.870
To first!

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:54.940
Safe!

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:05.720
<i>Yikes. They pulled one back and have
runners on second and third with one out.</i>

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:08.740
<i>If I messed up and put my team
in danger of giving up the lead,</i>

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:10.560
<i>I'd want to run away screaming.</i>

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:12.040
I'm sorry.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:14.380
Don't worry about it. 
Don't let it get to you.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:15.660
Put it behind you!

00:18:16.060 --> 00:18:16.800
Right.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:20.070
Play!

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:25.200
<i>They can't walk him to load the bases.
The next batter got a hit earlier.</i>

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.270
Ball!

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:29.420
<i>Crap.</i>

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.260
<i>All I'm seeing is nightmare scenarios.</i>

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:45.520
To third!

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.040
Out!

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:51.520
N-No way.

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:53.410
How is she so composed?!

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:54.680
That's impossible.

00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:58.070
Her heart must be all moldy
if it doesn't skip a beat with that!

00:18:58.070 --> 00:18:59.720
Nice one, Izumi!

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:04.060
"Observing is training, too," huh?

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:14.670
So, Hikaru, are you planning on 
joining a baseball team here?

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:20.740
No. I'm sure every team's busy
preparing for the summer tournament.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:23.290
So joining a team this late makes no sense.

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:25.750
So you'll pick it up in middle school, then?

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:29.050
Daigo-kun told me you'd
 written in your letter

00:19:29.050 --> 00:19:31.900
that you want to form 
a battery with him one day.

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:35.000
I wasn't being serious about that.

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:37.900
I only wrote it because it sounded good.

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:40.390
I'm not playing baseball ever again.

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:41.900
You...

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.910
Are you saying you lied to Daigo-kun?

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.270
That's right!

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:50.360
I mean, he's in Kanagawa and I'm in Gunma, 
so we'll never see each other again!

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:53.280
It's nearly impossible for us 
to play baseball together!

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:57.170
I actually... I actually want to...

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:03.100
But whatever. There's nothing I can do.

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:07.420
Hikaru.

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:09.350
Throw the ball.

00:20:10.530 --> 00:20:11.270
Huh?

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:13.330
You've been practicing, right?

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:15.270
Let me see your pitch.

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:23.480
Another one.

00:20:27.980 --> 00:20:30.580
Is this the pitch you wanted 
Daigo-kun to catch?

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:44.530
That was a good pitch.

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:47.470
Have you been practicing every day
over here as well?

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:52.480
You want to play baseball, right?

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:01.570
I do...

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:06.250
In reality, I wanted to keep playing
baseball with Daigo-kun and everyone else.

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:08.870
I had just started to love baseball!

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:11.140
If only I hadn't had to move!

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:12.830
If only I hadn't had to move...

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:19.350
I'm sorry, Hikaru.

00:21:19.950 --> 00:21:24.270
Your mother and I ended up
forcing you to sacrifice for us.

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:27.340
"I want to play baseball."

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:31.760
You weren't even able to utter 
that in earnest until now, huh?

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:35.430
But it's all right now.

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:39.770
You should be honest and 
do what you want to do.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:44.090
If it's something you want to do, 
both your mom and I will support it.

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:45.490
That's what we decided.

00:21:46.890 --> 00:21:47.750
But...

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:52.480
I was relieved to hear
you hadn't joined a team here yet.

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:54.280
Before I came over,

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:56.730
I called the Dolphins' manager,
Tashiro, to confirm something.

00:21:57.530 --> 00:21:58.540
Confirm what?

00:21:58.730 --> 00:22:03.380
That you're still registered as part 
of their team for the tournament.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:06.030
According to the rules,

00:22:06.030 --> 00:22:09.420
you can play in the matches as a member 
of the Dolphins, no matter where you live.

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:12.500
I'll pay for your train tickets.

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:15.520
If you want to play in the match 
on Sunday, hop on a train!

00:22:16.760 --> 00:22:18.640
R-Really?!

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:21.840
<i>And so, on Sunday...</i>

00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:30.030
Youth Rubber Baseball Tournament 
Kanagawa Tournament Arena

00:22:27.210 --> 00:22:29.690
<i>...the first day of the 
tournament had arrived!</i>

00:24:00.340 --> 00:24:02.170
The tournament's finally started!

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:05.040
What?! I'm hitting at the top of the order?!

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:08.670
All right! I'm going to shine here 
and make a name for myself!

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:10.910
H-Huh?

00:24:10.910 --> 00:24:15.470
Missing signs, making baserunning mistakes...
What am I doing?!

00:24:15.800 --> 00:24:19.120
Could it be that I have no baseball IQ?!

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:25.020
The Summer Tournament Begins!

00:24:19.700 --> 00:24:22.670
Next time: "The Summer Tournament Begins!"

00:24:22.670 --> 00:24:24.780
Run to the stage of your dreams!
